              LICENSE file at the commit above; the upstream repository does
              not ship a separate NOTICE file at this commit -- confirmed by
              reading its tree at the pinned commit, so none is reproduced
              here beyond this attribution).

Files in this directory derived from that notebook:

  - train_from_export.py: the DDP training script (torch.distributed /
    NCCL, RLCD+GRPO policy-gradient loss, AdamW parameter groups, cosine
    schedule, post-training temperature calibration) and the benchmark
    evaluation logic are copied from the notebook's cells with the minimal
    changes documented inline (each marked `# pointsman-change:`), primarily:
    reading a local pointsman dataset export (train/calibration/test.jsonl)
    instead of downloading the public `LocalLLaMA/typed-decisions` dataset,
    and using the export's own held-out calibration split instead of a
    slice of the training data.

This adaptation itself (the export-reading, manifest verification, and
tokenizer-admission-reporting code that is not present in the upstream
notebook) is part of pointsman and covered by this project's own
license (see the repository root). Where pointsman code and
Apache-2.0-licensed upstream code are combined in the same file, the
Apache-2.0 terms continue to apply to the reproduced upstream portions as
required by the License; see the SPDX-style header at the top of
train_from_export.py.

